--[[
	waves_test.luau — unit + oracle tests for `src/shared/sim/Waves.luau` and
	`src/shared/sim/Shop.luau` (`SIM-SPEC.md` §S1: transcription, not redesign).

	HOW TO RUN
	----------
	    cd roblox/test && luau -O2 waves_test.luau

	No arguments needed: `Content.luau` self-loads its embedded `content.json`,
	and the oracle vectors are embedded below. Exits non-zero on any failure.

	OPTIONALLY, a wider oracle dump can be handed in on argv. Standalone Luau has
	no file I/O, so it arrives as text, exactly as `parity.luau` does it: every
	trailing argument after `-a` is concatenated and parsed as a sequence of JSON
	documents, and the one carrying `hp_mult` is taken as the dump. Chunk it
	under the OS per-argument limit:

	    split -C 50000 dump.json /tmp/z.
	    args=(); for f in /tmp/z.*; do args+=("$(cat "$f")"); done
	    luau -O2 waves_test.luau -a "${args[@]}"

	THE ORACLE
	----------
	The expected values in `ORACLE_*` come from RUNNING THE RUST, never from
	hand-derivation (`CONTRACTS.md` C4's rule, applied to the sim layer). They
	were produced by a throwaway binary that only reads the sim crate's public
	surface: it calls `sim::step` with the weapons/enemies cleared each tick, so
	`rng_spawn` is advanced by `waves::spawn` alone and `s.enemies` after the
	step is exactly that tick's spawn list. `content::enemy_hp_mult` is `pub`,
	so the ramp curve is oracled directly.

	The per-tick `rng_spawn` state is the load-bearing assertion: `Rng.below` is
	a rejection loop that consumes a VARIABLE number of u32 words, so a state
	match over a contiguous 54,000-tick run proves the draw ORDER, COUNT and
	CONDITIONS all match the Rust (`SIM-SPEC.md` §S4). The same holds for
	`rng_shop` across successive offer generations.

	WHAT IS NOT TESTED HERE, AND WHY
	--------------------------------
	`Input::Reroll` and `Input::BuyOffer` live in `input.rs`, so by SIM-SPEC §S2
	they belong to `Input.luau`, not to `Shop.luau`. The reroll test below drives
	a LOCAL MIRROR of that branch structure (labelled as such) purely to prove
	the property `Shop.luau` owns: the offer stream advances exactly once per
	SUCCESSFUL reroll and not at all on the ignored branch.
]]

